    "updated_at": "2022-10-13T19:06:25Z",
    "body": "Thanks everyone for attending! Here are the notes from this meeting (the next one is at https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8385):\r\n\r\n### Agenda\r\n\r\n1. Review past action items\r\n    1. Emilio will ping the patch author for [focus delegate code seems wrongly only looking at children](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8157) or take over and send the patch to Olli.\r\n        1. Emilio pinged, probably this week we'll get the tests?\r\n    1. Domenic needs to do the spec work for [Define timing of focus fixup rule precisely when triggered by style changes](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8225).\r\n        1. Domenic still has not done this.\r\n        1. Let's let it drop off the action items list for now.\r\n    1. Emilio will send a PR to make [Intersection observer and mark paint timing steps run after (or during) \"update the rendering\", not before](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8277), including upstreaming ResizeObserver.\r\n        1. Done!\r\n    1. Joey will land a change to change Chromium's behavior around [Event bubbling on disabled form elements](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/5886).\r\n        1. Joey said he would try to land it, not sure if he did?\r\n    1. Emilio will add a spec change for [HTMLOptionsCollection length setter should specify what happens when you go over the option limit](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8337).\r\n        1. People on the call (which does not include Mason or Emilio today) think 100,000 is also fine, but we'll wait for Emilio.\r\n        1. Also nobody should do this. Official HTML triage call position.\r\n1. Carryovers from last time\r\n1. New topics\r\n    1. [Mike] Revisit [Is a general Script: editor a good idea?](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8321)\r\n        1. Couldn't find anything about the Link header being an antipattern, at least in TAG.\r\n        1. Some discussion about these types of headers from WebKit being problematic for serializability (i.e. save-to-disk). Also a problem with Link: rel=stylesheet.\r\n\r\n### Action Items\r\nNone\r\n",
